<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="110" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Invoice Review code page — lines, review pane, corrections, bulk, by-rule</title>
    <phase>4 Review and approval (WP4) — wave W4-3</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Frontend over server-enforced routes (100–102); authorization, totals and transitions live in the BFF, so the page is presentation and workflow.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Largest UI in the project: many interacting states (selection, pane, PDF highlight, bulk, by-rule, read-only), a prototype-to-production component mapping and a grid-framework decision.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P4-C</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>100, 101, 102, 108, 109</deps>
    <tags>frontend, code-page, fluent-ui</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-5 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Build the Invoice Review code page from the owner-reviewed prototype (layout A, D-58): header and totals, count filters, the lines grid with findings badge and value marks, the right pane (Review tab: findings, line decision as outcome cards, what was read with Correct, and the bounding-box document view), the By-rule view with "apply suggestion to n lines", bulk actions on ticked rows, Accept all clean lines, Pending shown as Processing, and read-only states — calling 100, 101 and 102.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE frontend developer. Expert in React code pages, Fluent UI v9, @spaarke/ui-components and @spaarke/auth.</role>

  <goal>A single-file web resource built from src/solutions/InvoiceReview/ that reproduces the prototype's review flow on real data with shared components, registers the Navigator side pane, leaves tab and action slots for 111, passes the ui-tests below including dark mode, and adds no npm package.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-31, FR-32 (adjustment lines shown; the add-adjustment step is in 111's approve wizard, as in the prototype), NFR-02, NFR-13, D-58. Reference (copy, never import): c:\code_files\spaarke-prototype\projects\ebilling.r1\ — README (answers 1–4, F-1, F-5, F-6, F-10), src\review\ ReviewPage, LinesGrid, LinePanel, RuleGroups, Dialogs (CorrectValueModal, BulkModal); screenshots\v1\. API: 100 (GET .../review, line decision routes), 101 (corrections, GET corrections), 102 (adjustment lines appear in the read model). Document bytes: GET /api/documents/{documentId}/content (Api/FileAccessEndpoints.cs:232). Skeleton to copy: src/solutions/CommunicationReconciliation/ (single-file vite build, renamed output; main.tsx imports resolveCodePageTheme, setupCodePageThemeListener, AppErrorBoundary, ensureNavigatorSidePane :51, called in a mount effect :194-196). Entry: the page is opened with an invoice id (URL or data envelope — copy the parsing pattern of src/solutions/sprk_invoicespage/src/main.tsx parseMatterId).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/solutions/InvoiceReview/ (index.html, package.json, vite.config.ts, tsconfig*.json, src/main.tsx, src/App.tsx, src/services/invoiceReviewApi.ts, src/components/)</file>
      <file role="read">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/FilePreview/ (108's PdfHighlightViewer)</file>
      <file role="read">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/ConsoleKit/ (109's StatusBar / RecordRow statusOverride; EvidenceLine for values read)</file>
      <file role="read">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/WorkspaceShell/ (MetricCard, MetricCardRow, types.ts MetricCardConfig), src/components/Worklist/laneCountFilters.ts (card-building example), src/components/SprkChat/OutcomeCard.tsx</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="100" status="pending">Read model and line decisions</dependency>
      <dependency task="101" status="pending">Corrections</dependency>
      <dependency task="102" status="pending">Adjustment lines and totals</dependency>
      <dependency task="108" status="pending">Bounding-box viewer</dependency>
      <dependency task="109" status="pending">ConsoleKit additions</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="task 109 (2026-10-15), ontology-r1 review">Run the visual ui-tests in light, dark and high-contrast on this page for statusOverride on StatusBar / RecordRow plus the reused components named in the "reuse" constraint below (MetricCard count filters, Accordion disclosure, outcome choice); task 109 covered statusOverride in Jest only. ConsoleKit gained ONLY statusOverride: OutcomeCards, CountFilters and Disclosure were removed after the review and must not be re-added.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md section 11, D-24, ontology-r1 review of task 109 (reuse; exact imports, all from @spaarke/ui-components unless noted)">Count filters (All, Processing, To decide, Clean, Decided): `import { MetricCardRow } from '@spaarke/ui-components'` (src/components/WorkspaceShell/MetricCardRow.tsx) fed `MetricCardConfig[]` (`import type { MetricCardConfig } from '@spaarke/ui-components'`, WorkspaceShell/types.ts:50). Per card: `selected` (aria-pressed, one selected), `value` (the count), `disableWhenEmpty: true` (count 0 disables the card; keep All enabled), `ariaLabel` "label, n lines", `onClick`; render MetricCardRow with layout="wide", ariaLabel "Line filters" and the cards array. Copy the card-building shape of src/components/Worklist/laneCountFilters.ts (buildLaneCountCards) into a page-local builder; do NOT add a new count-filter card component (D-24) and do not use StatTiles. Disclosure ("Why this was flagged", policy version, quoted clause, values read): Fluent v9 `import { Accordion, AccordionItem, AccordionHeader, AccordionPanel } from '@fluentui/react-components'` (collapsible, closed by default), as in src/components/ConsoleKit/RecordRow.tsx and src/components/DecisionWizard/steps/FoundStep.tsx in this tree and as src/components/Worklist/WorklistDisclosures.tsx does on branch task/ontology-059-worklist-widget (that file is not yet in this tree; do not depend on it). No custom Disclosure. Outcome choice (Your decision: Approve / Reduce / Disallow, suggestion first, body under the chosen option): `import { OutcomeCard } from '@spaarke/ui-components'` (src/components/SprkChat/OutcomeCard.tsx) is a read-only completion card driven by a server payload (IOutcomeCard), not a selector, so it does not fit the choice itself; build the choice from Fluent `import { RadioGroup, Radio } from '@fluentui/react-components'` (named group with an accessible name; arrow keys move selection; nothing happens until the single Confirm) and render the chosen option's body (reason, amount) in the page directly beneath it. OutcomeCard may be used to show the result of a confirmed decision if a server completion payload exists; otherwise use the decided StatusBar override. Status: `import { StatusBar, RecordRow, EvidenceLine } from '@spaarke/ui-components'` with the statusOverride prop (label, tone, optional description) (ConsoleKit/consoleStatus.ts ConsoleStatusOverride).</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 108 (2026-10-15)">PdfHighlightViewer (Spaarke.UI.Components FilePreview) was unit-tested with pdfjs faked; this task runs its three browser ui-tests (highlight, scroll-to-field, error/retry) against a real invoice PDF in the deployed code page, and confirms the Dataverse code-page CSP allows the pdfjs worker. If it does not, set GlobalWorkerOptions.workerSrc to a same-origin worker before the first load (the loader does not overwrite it).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012, prototype mapping">Shared components only (map, do not copy): PanelSplitter + useTwoPanelLayout (resizable right pane), PdfHighlightViewer (108) for DocumentView, StatusBar / RecordRow statusOverride (109), MetricCardRow + MetricCard for count filters, Fluent Accordion for disclosures and Fluent RadioGroup for the outcome choice (see the reuse constraint) for the kit.tsx pieces, EvidenceLine for values read, StatusBadge for line status, AiFieldTag for AI-coded fields, SprkModal FormModal for Correct value and bulk decide (ADR-050).</constraint>
    <constraint source="grid decision">The brief names the DataGrid framework, but it is FetchXML / config-driven (DataGrid.tsx:107-116 needs configId and an IDataverseClient; overrides are cell renderers only, configResolution.ts:41) and cannot take 100's read-model rows with selection, row ticks and per-value click. Use the Fluent v9 DataGrid primitive fed by the read model, no virtualization (F-5); record the decision in notes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021, F-10">Fluent v9 semantic tokens only; light, dark, high contrast; style a wrapper div, never the FluentProvider className.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-31, prototype answer 3">Correct (the reading is wrong; 101) and Reduce (the bill is wrong; 100) are separate affordances; a low-confidence value offers "Compare with the document, then confirm or correct".</constraint>
    <constraint source="F-1">Stored Pending is displayed as Processing (spinner, not decidable); the page refreshes while any line is Processing and stops when none is.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002, I-1">The page never computes totals or writes Dataverse; it shows the server's totals after each call.</constraint>
    <constraint source=".claude/patterns/webresource/full-page-custom-page.md, ADR-028">Single self-contained HTML; guarded Xrm access; initAuth before render; BFF calls through authenticatedFetch; ensureNavigatorSidePane() on mount.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-12">No new npm package; npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund.</constraint>
  </constraints>

