    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Code page skeleton" location="src/solutions/CommunicationReconciliation/src/main.tsx">Theme, auth, error boundary, Navigator registration.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Layout A" location="c:\code_files\spaarke-prototype\projects\ebilling.r1\src\review\ReviewPage.tsx">Grid left, pane right via PanelSplitter + useTwoPanelLayout.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Scaffold src/solutions/InvoiceReview/ from CommunicationReconciliation (output name directional: sprk_invoicereviewpage.html); npm install with the flags above.</step>
    <step order="2">API client for 100 / 101 / 102 with ProblemDetails handling (stable code shown; 403 makes the page read-only; ebilling.disabled shows a disabled notice).</step>
    <step order="3">Header (firm, invoice and tracking number, core record link, period, date, status), totals strip, count filters as MetricCardRow (All, Processing, To decide, Clean, Decided).</step>
    <step order="4">Lines grid: status, date, timekeeper (unmatched mark), narrative, hours, amount, findings badge (severity and count, hover lists rules), approved; low-confidence value mark; AI-observation mark; row tick; clicking a value selects the line and highlights that field on the PDF.</step>
    <step order="5">Right pane, Review tab: findings (rule, message, suggestion; Accordion reveal for policy version, quoted clause and values read), Your decision (Fluent RadioGroup, suggestion first, one Confirm, then move to the next line to decide), What was read (EvidenceLine rows with Correct), decided state (StatusBar override), PdfHighlightViewer below scrolled to the line. Leave a tab slot for 111 (Context, Related work, History).</step>
    <step order="6">By-rule view (groups by rule, most severe first, then count) with "Apply suggestion to n lines" through the multi-line route; action bar: Accept all clean lines (n), Accept / Disallow on ticked rows (FormModal, one reason), progress, and a "Decide invoice" button slot for 111.</step>
    <step order="7">States: loading, all clean, heavily flagged, low-confidence value, unmatched timekeeper, decided read-only, viewer without write access (read-only), 150 lines.</step>
    <step order="8">npm run build; check the single-file output; run the ui-tests below against dev after 112 deploys (or a local server with a mocked API for visual checks); record results.</step>
    <step order="9">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell to "✅ [done]".</step>
    <step order="10">Record deviations (web resource name, grid decision, any prototype behaviour not reproduced) in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the page needs a navigation entry (sitemap subarea, invoice form command or view command) it is a solution change: do not edit src/dataverse/solutions/SpaarkeMaster/**; record the need for 112.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a needed shared component is missing or a prototype behaviour needs a new shared component beyond 108 / 109 and the reuse constraint, STOP and propose it with a section 11 justification; never copy from the prototype repository.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the owner requires the DataGrid framework for the lines grid, STOP: it needs a read-model data source added to the framework first.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Spec section 11 row "Invoice Review and Rule Review code pages" (overlap sprk_invoicespage, a matter invoice grid); no invoice review page exists (Glob src/solutions/*).</existing>
    <extension>sprk_invoicespage stays the list; review needs a per-invoice workspace with the document. The page composes shared components (108, 109 and existing kit) rather than adding new ones.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Reviewers cannot decide lines, correct values or see sources, so FR-31 and success criterion 4 fail.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Page renders and registers Navigator">
      <url>https://{org}.crm.dynamics.com/main.aspx?appid={app-id}&amp;pagetype=webresource&amp;webresourceName=sprk_invoicereviewpage&amp;data=invoiceId%3D{id}</url>
      <steps>
        <step>Open an In Review invoice as a user with write access</step>
        <step>Verify header, totals, count cards and grid load, the document shows page 1, and the Navigator side pane is docked</step>
        <step>Check the console for errors</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Layout A as in prototype screenshots v1; no console errors</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Decide a flagged line">
      <steps>
        <step>Start with the first line to decide; choose the suggested Reduce; confirm with a reason</step>
        <step>Verify totals update from the server and the next line to decide is selected</step>
        <step>Try Reduce without a reason; verify the server error is shown and nothing changes</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Matches prototype walkthrough step 2</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Correct a misread value">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a line with a low-confidence hours value; click the value; verify the PDF boxes that field</step>
        <step>Correct the hours; verify findings clear, the line becomes Clean, and the correction is distinct from a Reduce</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Matches prototype walkthrough step 3</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Bulk, by rule, read-only, Processing">
      <steps>
        <step>Accept all clean lines; in By rule apply a suggestion to several lines; tick rows and Disallow with one reason</step>
        <step>Open as a read-only user: no decision or correction affordances</step>
        <step>Open an invoice with Pending lines: they show Processing and are not decidable</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>One server request per bulk action; read-only view; F-1 label</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021, F-4)">
      <steps>
        <step>Switch the app theme to dark</step>
        <step>Verify no white backgrounds or black text in header, grid, pane, modals; badges legible</step>
        <step>Verify the PDF page stays light and its highlight boxes stay visible</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Tokens only; page light in dark mode</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">install, build</tool>
    <tool name="ui-test">browser checks via the ui-test skill</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/solutions/InvoiceReview/</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">npm run build produces one self-contained HTML file; package.json adds no dependency beyond the copied skeleton's.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every 100 / 101 route is reachable from the page and the page reflects server results, including ProblemDetails errors.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Correct and Reduce are separate affordances; clicking a value highlights that field on the PDF.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Pending lines show Processing and cannot be decided; a 403 makes the page read-only; ebilling.disabled shows a notice.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The prototype-to-shared mapping in the constraints is used; no file imports from the prototype repository; the grid decision is recorded.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ensureNavigatorSidePane() is called on mount; no file under src/dataverse/solutions/SpaarkeMaster/ changed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The ui-tests above pass, including dark mode; a 150-line invoice opens in under 3 s in dev (measured in 112).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>P4-C with 052 and 104: no file overlap. 111 adds the Context / Related work / History tabs, the header "Awaiting" approvers (103), the invoice decision wizard and the blocked-submission state into this page's slots. Deployment and the navigation entry are 112's.</notes>

